From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 06:43:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] graphicscapture: Capture composition visuals.

Office's AirSpace captures a visual for its grid animations with
GraphicsCaptureItem.CreateFromVisual, a free-threaded
Direct3D11CaptureFramePool and a session, and fails fast on nearly any
unexpected answer along the way; without the class it took another
path.

An item takes a visual of Wine's composition, and has its size.  A pool
keeps its buffers on the device it was made with; a buffer is free,
drawn into, ready, or held by a frame until the frame is closed.  Each
frame drawn raises FrameArrived once, on the thread pool for a pool made
free-threaded, through the dispatcher queue of the thread that made it
otherwise.  A session draws the item into the pool from StartCapture
until closed.  Windows and displays cannot be captured yet, and
IsSupported still says so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

